[[:db/retract 17592186176212 :question/answer-fields 17592186173530] {:db/id 17592186175980 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e0057193-1fc8-5f60-b2e8-92515ea3b1e6" "question-795a5978-6945-51dd-9230-522e60fb9dd8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186175996 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-0071fbbf-507b-5e86-9e07-511fe6080666"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186175979 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1d2fc887-f2a2-5a12-af93-46ac7487f8f4" "question-b3090cbd-55f4-50b9-b96a-e12ca57ae315"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176065 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-139ae790-9731-55fc-ab5e-266ae6726353" "question-3a9f44f1-362f-50d2-bbcf-0383dfbcd3ea"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e0057193-1fc8-5f60-b2e8-92515ea3b1e6" :question/id #uuid "e0057193-1fc8-5f60-b2e8-92515ea3b1e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-161153" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the part of the plane $z=2\\sqrt{5}x+2y$ that is bounded by the constraints $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{5}x+2y,\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2.\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2\\sqrt{5}x+2y)=2\\sqrt{5}, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\sqrt{5}x+2y)=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(2\\sqrt{5})}^{2}+(2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+20+4}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{25}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =5{∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =5\\cdot (1-(-1))\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-989c6007-badd-544d-87f7-194be590ca1c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-989c6007-badd-544d-87f7-194be590ca1c" :answer-field/id #uuid "989c6007-badd-544d-87f7-194be590ca1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f20ee68d-f941-5858-910c-aad522ef84b9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b9882397-20a7-55a5-b9af-85aae783bc47" "answer-f20ee68d-f941-5858-910c-aad522ef84b9" "answer-96e2a9a0-2d62-5a79-a93d-b7db07b18154" "answer-fcddb203-3aef-5988-8495-b140e1e4214e" "answer-03199862-16b9-557b-8bef-764c1954ae8a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9882397-20a7-55a5-b9af-85aae783bc47" :answer/id #uuid "b9882397-20a7-55a5-b9af-85aae783bc47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f20ee68d-f941-5858-910c-aad522ef84b9" :answer/id #uuid "f20ee68d-f941-5858-910c-aad522ef84b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96e2a9a0-2d62-5a79-a93d-b7db07b18154" :answer/id #uuid "96e2a9a0-2d62-5a79-a93d-b7db07b18154" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fcddb203-3aef-5988-8495-b140e1e4214e" :answer/id #uuid "fcddb203-3aef-5988-8495-b140e1e4214e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03199862-16b9-557b-8bef-764c1954ae8a" :answer/id #uuid "03199862-16b9-557b-8bef-764c1954ae8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-795a5978-6945-51dd-9230-522e60fb9dd8" :question/id #uuid "795a5978-6945-51dd-9230-522e60fb9dd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-161129" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of $z=3{x}^{2}-y$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=3{x}^{2}-y,\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 2.\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3{x}^{2}-y)=6x, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3{x}^{2}-y)=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(6x)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+36{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{2+36{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\sqrt{2+36{x}^{2}}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9ec2bea1-f597-57e9-8493-155da2b72ca3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9ec2bea1-f597-57e9-8493-155da2b72ca3" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ec2bea1-f597-57e9-8493-155da2b72ca3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-944324b3-9b00-578a-a869-20197fc9cd6b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7853d8da-02ca-52fe-82ab-8d3e95436d1c" "answer-d52761a0-f3c2-5486-8780-7ee4cfd846a1" "answer-a7727358-0e8f-5186-a4f4-a4093c7f5305" "answer-1aa6f07d-e7c8-523d-bd08-943563edb16a" "answer-944324b3-9b00-578a-a869-20197fc9cd6b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7853d8da-02ca-52fe-82ab-8d3e95436d1c" :answer/id #uuid "7853d8da-02ca-52fe-82ab-8d3e95436d1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+18{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d52761a0-f3c2-5486-8780-7ee4cfd846a1" :answer/id #uuid "d52761a0-f3c2-5486-8780-7ee4cfd846a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1+9{x}^{4}+{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7727358-0e8f-5186-a4f4-a4093c7f5305" :answer/id #uuid "a7727358-0e8f-5186-a4f4-a4093c7f5305" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{1+6{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1aa6f07d-e7c8-523d-bd08-943563edb16a" :answer/id #uuid "1aa6f07d-e7c8-523d-bd08-943563edb16a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{1+9{x}^{4}+{y}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-944324b3-9b00-578a-a869-20197fc9cd6b" :answer/id #uuid "944324b3-9b00-578a-a869-20197fc9cd6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2+36{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176212 :question/problem "Find the surface area of the portion of the surface $z=2y+{x}^{2}$ whose projection onto the $xy$-plane is bounded by $y=8x,$ $x=1,$ and the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=2y+{x}^{2},\\,(x,y)\\in D\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 8x},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/d2/d2ca6ee66367bd86cd56fe3a4891dbd4b64d9e23d5b4d97c9650b3af184b423f.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y+{x}^{2})=2x, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y+{x}^{2})=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(2x)^{2}+(2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{5+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{8x}\\sqrt{5+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{5+4{x}^{2}}\\cdot y\\,{|}_{0}^{8x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}8x\\sqrt{5+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $u=5+4{x}^{2},$ we get $\\text{d}u=8x\\,\\text{d}x.$ Also, the limits must be changed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & 1 \\\\ u & 5 & 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSubstituting these into our integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}8x\\sqrt{5+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{5}^{9}{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}\\,{|}_{5}^{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({9}^{3/2}-{5}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(27-5\\sqrt{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-70853f79-e38b-5582-8553-bedada3f4f29"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-70853f79-e38b-5582-8553-bedada3f4f29" :answer-field/id #uuid "70853f79-e38b-5582-8553-bedada3f4f29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5269f1b8-3177-521a-9c3f-e7af2b0e1033" :answer-field/choices ["answer-da7205c0-5e4b-57ab-a38b-f26734714a73" "answer-5269f1b8-3177-521a-9c3f-e7af2b0e1033" "answer-a1ae44f3-7378-59c0-9c18-c2dc952a1624" "answer-e0f309e2-670c-56fd-85d1-55d851f737f4" "answer-1b05d304-e890-5571-a95a-08cab23c0431"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da7205c0-5e4b-57ab-a38b-f26734714a73" :answer/id #uuid "da7205c0-5e4b-57ab-a38b-f26734714a73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5269f1b8-3177-521a-9c3f-e7af2b0e1033" :answer/id #uuid "5269f1b8-3177-521a-9c3f-e7af2b0e1033" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}(27-5\\sqrt{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1ae44f3-7378-59c0-9c18-c2dc952a1624" :answer/id #uuid "a1ae44f3-7378-59c0-9c18-c2dc952a1624" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}(3-\\sqrt{5})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0f309e2-670c-56fd-85d1-55d851f737f4" :answer/id #uuid "e0f309e2-670c-56fd-85d1-55d851f737f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}(8-2\\sqrt{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1b05d304-e890-5571-a95a-08cab23c0431" :answer/id #uuid "1b05d304-e890-5571-a95a-08cab23c0431" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-0071fbbf-507b-5e86-9e07-511fe6080666" :question/id #uuid "0071fbbf-507b-5e86-9e07-511fe6080666" :question/math-academy-id "q-161183" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the portion of the surface $z=\\frac{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3}$ whose projection onto the $xy$-plane is bounded by $y=\\sqrt{1+4x}$ and the $x$-axis from $x=0$ to $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=\\frac{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3},\\,(x,y)\\in D\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1+4x}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/9a/9a459a9807befc312528771626dca293a7ebbccd97a2c1e938f47a2d90a36726.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3})=2\\sqrt{x}, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3})=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(2\\sqrt{x})}^{2}+(0)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+4x}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{1+4x}}\\sqrt{1+4x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4x}\\cdot y\\,{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{1+4x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{1+4x}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(1+4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x+2{x}^{2})\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(2+8)-0 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e4962c93-3582-5793-94a8-d5e64919a899"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e4962c93-3582-5793-94a8-d5e64919a899" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4962c93-3582-5793-94a8-d5e64919a899" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3f58fbfa-2a3c-5f8a-8c15-ac63c162c8c4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3f58fbfa-2a3c-5f8a-8c15-ac63c162c8c4" "answer-e8895199-6569-5bad-a980-9e6b74e4814d" "answer-26f6af28-58a5-5980-8be5-d39c9b4b3514" "answer-b6449307-a0ba-56cc-a5f1-291146f541f9" "answer-9c2e9088-2863-5032-aa2c-88ec65760072"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f58fbfa-2a3c-5f8a-8c15-ac63c162c8c4" :answer/id #uuid "3f58fbfa-2a3c-5f8a-8c15-ac63c162c8c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8895199-6569-5bad-a980-9e6b74e4814d" :answer/id #uuid "e8895199-6569-5bad-a980-9e6b74e4814d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26f6af28-58a5-5980-8be5-d39c9b4b3514" :answer/id #uuid "26f6af28-58a5-5980-8be5-d39c9b4b3514" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b6449307-a0ba-56cc-a5f1-291146f541f9" :answer/id #uuid "b6449307-a0ba-56cc-a5f1-291146f541f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c2e9088-2863-5032-aa2c-88ec65760072" :answer/id #uuid "9c2e9088-2863-5032-aa2c-88ec65760072" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1d2fc887-f2a2-5a12-af93-46ac7487f8f4" :question/id #uuid "1d2fc887-f2a2-5a12-af93-46ac7487f8f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161442" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(x,z)\\,:\\,\\boxed{}\\,}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the part of the cone $y=4\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}$ that lies inside the cylinder ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}.$ From left to right, what are the missing expressions?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $y=f(x,z)$ with $(x,z)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\ny=4\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}},\\,{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le \\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂y}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}})=\\frac{4x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}})=\\frac{4z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{4x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}})}^{2}+{(\\frac{4z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{16{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}+\\frac{16{z}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{\\frac{17({x}^{2}+{z}^{2})}{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{17}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is\n\n$\\,$ $\\sqrt{17}\\,$ and $\\,{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le \\frac{1}{4}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7b2b5a8a-3d1e-588b-a0ea-de39882b51aa"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7b2b5a8a-3d1e-588b-a0ea-de39882b51aa" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b2b5a8a-3d1e-588b-a0ea-de39882b51aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f8918b25-32d9-5a19-ba97-973014cfd089" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1735e166-5acc-5324-851d-91faeb7a9618" "answer-3369dcb6-e91a-5e4b-b5d1-596236417674" "answer-d803556f-449c-5597-ae86-ae738f26a508" "answer-4ba101ca-c17d-55ee-8ca8-392a0b3b4fd5" "answer-f8918b25-32d9-5a19-ba97-973014cfd089"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1735e166-5acc-5324-851d-91faeb7a9618" :answer/id #uuid "1735e166-5acc-5324-851d-91faeb7a9618" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4\\,$ and $\\,{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3369dcb6-e91a-5e4b-b5d1-596236417674" :answer/id #uuid "3369dcb6-e91a-5e4b-b5d1-596236417674" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{1+\\frac{16(x+y)}{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,$ and $\\,y\\ge 2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d803556f-449c-5597-ae86-ae738f26a508" :answer/id #uuid "d803556f-449c-5597-ae86-ae738f26a508" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{1+\\frac{16}{{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,$ and $\\,y\\le 2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ba101ca-c17d-55ee-8ca8-392a0b3b4fd5" :answer/id #uuid "4ba101ca-c17d-55ee-8ca8-392a0b3b4fd5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{1+\\frac{16}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{16}{{y}^{2}}}\\,$ and $\\,{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}<4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8918b25-32d9-5a19-ba97-973014cfd089" :answer/id #uuid "f8918b25-32d9-5a19-ba97-973014cfd089" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\sqrt{17}\\,$ and $\\,{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le \\frac{1}{4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b3090cbd-55f4-50b9-b96a-e12ca57ae315" :question/id #uuid "b3090cbd-55f4-50b9-b96a-e12ca57ae315" :question/math-academy-id "q-161226" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the part of the plane $x=\\frac{y-z}{3}$ whose projection onto the $yz$-plane is bounded by the constraints $1\\le y\\le 4$ and $1\\le z\\le 3.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $x=f(y,z)$ with $(y,z)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂y})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{y-z}{3},\\,(y,z)\\in D,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 4,\\,1\\le z\\le 3},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/3f/3f06a9c686a935cb6c561affbcd224045618d9cacaf94eb7c9eab8a9ca8da44c.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{y-z}{3})=\\frac{1}{3}, \\\\ \\frac{∂x}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{y-z}{3})=-\\frac{1}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂y})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂x}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{9}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{9}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{3}{∬}_{D}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{3}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{3}\\cdot (4-1)\\cdot (3-1) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-05c69fee-4df2-5b99-a8fc-ad508d7794be"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-05c69fee-4df2-5b99-a8fc-ad508d7794be" :answer-field/id #uuid "05c69fee-4df2-5b99-a8fc-ad508d7794be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3a4ce4b5-b090-52fb-8521-91a7d5fb6e64" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3a4ce4b5-b090-52fb-8521-91a7d5fb6e64" "answer-c3100f75-563f-5f1f-9d25-aade507ac5a0" "answer-5c5b7aca-0852-5446-be6b-4b27132d1d3a" "answer-bb48da7b-7426-5584-96a0-a5b3e5a67853" "answer-89d97de7-0a07-5bd0-a64a-ce2c1b74eb86"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a4ce4b5-b090-52fb-8521-91a7d5fb6e64" :answer/id #uuid "3a4ce4b5-b090-52fb-8521-91a7d5fb6e64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3100f75-563f-5f1f-9d25-aade507ac5a0" :answer/id #uuid "c3100f75-563f-5f1f-9d25-aade507ac5a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c5b7aca-0852-5446-be6b-4b27132d1d3a" :answer/id #uuid "5c5b7aca-0852-5446-be6b-4b27132d1d3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb48da7b-7426-5584-96a0-a5b3e5a67853" :answer/id #uuid "bb48da7b-7426-5584-96a0-a5b3e5a67853" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-89d97de7-0a07-5bd0-a64a-ce2c1b74eb86" :answer/id #uuid "89d97de7-0a07-5bd0-a64a-ce2c1b74eb86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{11}{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-139ae790-9731-55fc-ab5e-266ae6726353" :question/id #uuid "139ae790-9731-55fc-ab5e-266ae6726353" :question/math-academy-id "q-109765" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the part of the surface $z=xy$ that is subject to the constraint ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\nz=xy,\\,(x,y)\\in D\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 1},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/f0/f0faa92e0f89c86248abffad7f61cac5d94a3848a7f7be4464c4b28d3915aa32.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)=y, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy)=x,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(y)^{2}+(x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region $D$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 1,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula for polar coordinates, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\sqrt{1+{r}^{2}}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{1}r\\sqrt{1+{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{1}r\\sqrt{1+{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}r\\sqrt{1+{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $u=1+{r}^{2},$ we get $\\text{d}u=2r\\,\\text{d}r.$ Also, the limits must be changed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & 0 & 1 \\\\ u & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSubstituting these into our integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}r\\sqrt{1+{r}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}r & =2\\pi \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{2}{u}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot {[\\frac{2}{3}\\,{u}^{3/2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}{[{u}^{3/2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}[{2}^{3/2}-1] \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi (2\\sqrt{2}-1)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c42dd57a-1d8c-5adc-b40d-c45195678c1d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c42dd57a-1d8c-5adc-b40d-c45195678c1d" :answer-field/id #uuid "c42dd57a-1d8c-5adc-b40d-c45195678c1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-543c20d4-2012-58fc-988d-4183a7a0d1bb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4281a994-2dee-5d00-a661-565bf6f7aacd" "answer-134a8ec5-3c99-5a35-b135-9550a1a589e4" "answer-f67ff004-d369-5080-8ecc-4238d9b7be10" "answer-543c20d4-2012-58fc-988d-4183a7a0d1bb" "answer-0d1c8e0a-12da-57b1-b178-119e2ed0094c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4281a994-2dee-5d00-a661-565bf6f7aacd" :answer/id #uuid "4281a994-2dee-5d00-a661-565bf6f7aacd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi (\\sqrt{3}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-134a8ec5-3c99-5a35-b135-9550a1a589e4" :answer/id #uuid "134a8ec5-3c99-5a35-b135-9550a1a589e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi -1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f67ff004-d369-5080-8ecc-4238d9b7be10" :answer/id #uuid "f67ff004-d369-5080-8ecc-4238d9b7be10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-543c20d4-2012-58fc-988d-4183a7a0d1bb" :answer/id #uuid "543c20d4-2012-58fc-988d-4183a7a0d1bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi (2\\sqrt{2}-1)}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d1c8e0a-12da-57b1-b178-119e2ed0094c" :answer/id #uuid "0d1c8e0a-12da-57b1-b178-119e2ed0094c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi \\sqrt{14}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3a9f44f1-362f-50d2-bbcf-0383dfbcd3ea" :question/id #uuid "3a9f44f1-362f-50d2-bbcf-0383dfbcd3ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-161175" :question/problem "Find the surface area of the part of the plane $y=3x+2z$ that is subject to the constraints ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le 16,\\,x\\le 0$ and $z\\ge 0.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ defined by $y=f(x,z)$ with $(x,z)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn this case, our surface is given by\n\n$$\ny=3x+2z,\\,(x,z)\\in D\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le 16,\\,x\\le 0,\\,z\\ge 0},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/48/48ffe2b0bd40937205d9b9d3b6cc264f83bd56ea30a5df318ba7c7507efb68f7.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂y}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3x+2z)=3, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3x+2z)=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nthe surface area is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂y}{∂z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(3)^{2}+(2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+9+4}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{14}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region $D$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,0\\le r\\le 4,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi }.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula for polar coordinates, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{14}\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}\\sqrt{14}\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{4}r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta {\\int }_{0}^{4}r\\,\\text{d}r \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}\\cdot [\\theta ]_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }\\cdot {[\\frac{{r}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =4\\pi \\sqrt{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b2bc578f-8afe-5a87-8c83-39f18d34c660"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b2bc578f-8afe-5a87-8c83-39f18d34c660" :answer-field/id #uuid "b2bc578f-8afe-5a87-8c83-39f18d34c660" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cf2a1588-1e59-59e9-802e-6ebad0b0fea0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c4b6f195-b9dc-56ca-a43b-6af6cf36c33b" "answer-b4f9a248-c377-505f-ac3a-9e96059ce3f5" "answer-cf2a1588-1e59-59e9-802e-6ebad0b0fea0" "answer-3dc37952-1697-5509-8bc7-6ccd85ec6880" "answer-aea19d27-cea1-5633-a35f-860030bc1eeb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c4b6f195-b9dc-56ca-a43b-6af6cf36c33b" :answer/id #uuid "c4b6f195-b9dc-56ca-a43b-6af6cf36c33b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi \\sqrt{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4f9a248-c377-505f-ac3a-9e96059ce3f5" :answer/id #uuid "b4f9a248-c377-505f-ac3a-9e96059ce3f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi (\\sqrt{17}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf2a1588-1e59-59e9-802e-6ebad0b0fea0" :answer/id #uuid "cf2a1588-1e59-59e9-802e-6ebad0b0fea0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi \\sqrt{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3dc37952-1697-5509-8bc7-6ccd85ec6880" :answer/id #uuid "3dc37952-1697-5509-8bc7-6ccd85ec6880" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\pi \\sqrt{14}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aea19d27-cea1-5633-a35f-860030bc1eeb" :answer/id #uuid "aea19d27-cea1-5633-a35f-860030bc1eeb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi (\\sqrt{14}-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176989 :tutorial/content "Recall that if $S$ is a surface parametrized by a differentiable vector-valued function\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle x(u,v), \\: y(u,v), \\: z(u,v) \\big\\rangle\n$$\n\ndefined over a region $D$ in the $uv$-plane, then the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{S} \\: \\textrm{d}S =  \\iint\\limits_{D} \\| \\mathbf{r}'_ u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v  \\| \\: \\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{r}'_ u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v$ is the fundamental vector product of the surface.\n\nNow, if our surface $S$ is defined as $z= f(x,y),$ then it can always be parameterized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(x,y)= \\left\\langle x,\\: y,\\: f(x,y)\\right\\rangle  \\qquad (x,y)  \\in D.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the variables $x$ and $y$ act as parameters. \n\nThus, the fundamental vector product of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\frac{∂f}{∂x} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{∂f}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂f}{∂y},\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand using the fact that $z = f(x,y),$ we can write this as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′} & =⟨-\\frac{∂z}{∂x},\\,-\\frac{∂z}{∂y},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\| \\mathbf{r}'_ u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v  \\| = \\sqrt{1 + \\left(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial x}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial y}\\right)^2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that for a surface $S$ defined by $z=f(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\,  \\text{d}S = \\iint\\limits_D \\sqrt{1+\\left(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial x}\\right)^2+\\left(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial y}\\right)^2} \\: \\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the projection of $S$ onto the $xy$-plane.\n\nLet's look at an example of how to apply this formula." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176990 :tutorial/content "![](images/86/867722106ffd8445b62a98ab43197ac2fba646faff95017ef7e92c254a97fb6e.png)\n\n  \n\nThe surface $S$ shown above consists of the part of the paraboloid $z=x^2+y^2$ that lies under the plane $z=9.$ Let's compute the surface area of $S.$\n\nThe plane intersects the paraboloid when $z=9.$ Thus, the curve that describes the intersection points is\n\n$$\nx^2+y^2 = 9,\n$$\n\nwhich is a circle of radius $3$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nTherefore, our surface can be described by the equations\n\n$$\nz = f(x,y) = x^2 + y^2, \\quad (x,y) \\in D\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{(x,y): \\, x^2 + y^2 \\le 9\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the surface area of $S,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\,  \\text{d}S = \\iint\\limits_D \\sqrt{1+\\left(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial x}\\right)^2+\\left(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial y}\\right)^2} \\: \\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2x, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these expressions into our surface area formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+(2x)^{2}+(2y)^{2}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}}\\,dA.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by changing the variables to polar coordinates $(x,y)\\to (r,\\theta),$ we have $\\textrm dA = r\\,\\textrm d r\\, \\textrm d \\theta.$ Thus, our integration region becomes\n\n$$\n\\Delta = \\left\\{(r,\\theta): \\, 0\\leq r\\leq 3,\\:0\\leq\\theta\\lt 2\\pi\\right\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+4{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}}\\,dA & ={∬}_{Δ}\\sqrt{1+4(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+4(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}}\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}r\\sqrt{1+4{r}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )}\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}r\\sqrt{1+4{r}^{2}}\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3}r\\sqrt{1+4{r}^{2}\\,}\\,dr\\,d\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,d\\theta \\,{\\int }_{0}^{3}r\\sqrt{1+4{r}^{2}\\,}\\,dr \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{3}r\\sqrt{1+4{r}^{2}\\,}\\,dr \\\\  & =2\\pi {[\\frac{1}{12}{(1+4{r}^{2})}^{3/2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}{[{(1+4{r}^{2})}^{3/2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}(37\\sqrt{37}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that the area of our surface is \n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\,  \\text{d}S =  \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}(37\\sqrt{37} -1).\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186176142 :activity/expected-seconds 1140.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
